      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Challenger's review of the claim against the Bay 3 daily ledger for 14 Oct 2026 (RW-114, stretch hood film):\n\nNet dispatches: ORD-7781 (8) + ORD-7784 (5) + ORD-7790 (6) + ORD-7792 (4) = 23 units.\nReceipts: GRN-3301 (6) + GRN-3303 (5) + GRN-3304 (6) = 17 units.\nORD-7788 (7 units, 09:48) is annotated as cancelled at 10:02 with the units returned to the bin and the movement reversed, so it carries no net effect; even counted gross, dispatches (30) would still exceed receipts (17).\n\nThe closing figure reconciles independently: 52 opening - 23 + 17 = 46 rolls, matching both the 22:00 system closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46. RW-209 also reconciles (310 + 40 - 12 = 338).\n\nOn this evidence the claim that Riverside dispatched more units of RW-114 than it received on 14 October is supported. I am not challenging it.",
          "content_hash": "0x7f145696a8d2ecd99a53146ea2e4f9d0c8bb29d62b2abe12f79f7377152b7cf6",
          "created_at_ms": 1793325520065,
          "message_id": "fc7e2947-fe43-446c-a2e4-fdbb75c81d9f",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 independent check of the ledger, done from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nRW-114 movements 14 Oct: dispatches ORD-7781 8, ORD-7784 5, ORD-7790 6, ORD-7792 4 = 23 units; receipts GRN-3301 6, GRN-3303 5, GRN-3304 6 = 17 units. 23 > 17, so the claim's wording (dispatched more than received) holds on net figures.\n\nORD-7788 (-7, 09:48) is annotated cancelled 10:02 with units returned and the movement reversed, so I exclude it from net totals. Treating it as gross instead gives 30 vs 17, so the direction of the comparison is the same either way; only the magnitude is uncertain.\n\nReconciliation supports the same reading: 52 + 17 - 23 = 46 rolls at 22:00, matching the recorded closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count. RW-209: 310 + 40 - 12 = 338, also consistent. I find no unsupported element in the claim and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x65aa1285f913c4c59d159c61020b18f22ff01479c01d72089ccd42fc3321c368",
          "created_at_ms": 1793325542643,
          "message_id": "2f6899ff-586d-45a6-8247-491e70b7472d",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent check of the 14 Oct Bay 3 ledger, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nRW-114 dispatches: ORD-7781 8 + ORD-7784 5 + ORD-7790 6 + ORD-7792 4 = 23 units. Receipts: GRN-3301 6 + GRN-3303 5 + GRN-3304 6 = 17 units. 23 > 17, so the claim as worded holds.\n\nI exclude ORD-7788 (-7) from net totals: it is annotated cancelled at 10:02 with units returned to the bin and the movement reversed. Counting it gross would give 30 vs 17, so the direction of the comparison is unchanged; only the magnitude is uncertain, and I note that uncertainty.\n\nReconciliation: 52 opening + 17 received - 23 dispatched = 46 rolls at 22:00, which matches both the recorded closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46. RW-209 also reconciles: 310 + 40 - 12 = 338. I find no discrepancy and no unsupported element in the claim.",
          "content_hash": "0x95aad0d5bd9022794b5c466da8c00adfbde3d3e26a5b0cb3e5916a35c184122a",
          "created_at_ms": 1793325608392,
          "message_id": "989e75d2-cbdb-4ace-ae94-ae4b045839b2",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent check of the 14 Oct Bay 3 ledger, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nRW-114 dispatches: ORD-7781 8 + ORD-7784 5 + ORD-7790 6 + ORD-7792 4 = 23 units. Receipts: GRN-3301 6 + GRN-3303 5 + GRN-3304 6 = 17 units. 23 > 17, so the claim as worded holds.\n\nORD-7788 (-7, 09:48) is annotated cancelled at 10:02 with units returned to the bin and the movement reversed, so I exclude it from net totals. Counting it gross gives 30 vs 17: same direction, different magnitude, and I note that as the only uncertainty in the claim.\n\nReconciliation: 52 opening + 17 received - 23 dispatched = 46 rolls at 22:00, matching both the recorded closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46. RW-209 also reconciles: 310 + 40 - 12 = 338. I find no discrepancy and no unsupported element in the claim, and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x87f6ead3a23842ab3591fff964ae07af6cbfb01c82b65f648c4570547943652b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793325651095,
